<title>GERMANY: Bavaria Sept CPI down 0.1 pct, up 1.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Bavaria Sept CPI down 0.1 pct, up 1.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state statistics office in the German state of Bavaria reported the following consumer price changes for September.</p>
<p>    Cost of living		September	   August</p>
<p>    Month/month (pct change)  -0.1		  -0.1</p>
<p>    Year/year		     +1.3		  +1.3</p>
<p>NOTE - This data is combined with data from three other major German states to calculate the preliminary figure for the whole of west Germany.</p>
<p>Bavaria gave the following breakdown of its September cost of living data:</p>
<p>    Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr Index</p>
<p>    Overall price index		     - 0.1     + 1.3 114.4</p>
<p>    Rents					 + 0.5     + 3.0 127.0</p>
<p>    Household energy			  +16.2     +26.8 100.9</p>
<p>    Personal goods, services and other  - 3.3     + 0.7 124.1</p>
<p>    Transport and communications	  + 0.2     + 1.6 115.7</p>
<p>    Furniture and other household goods 0.0	 + 0.7 109.7</p>
<p>    Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   - 0.4     + 0.5 108.0</p>
<p>    Clothing, shoes			   0.0	 + 0.8 106.7</p>
<p>    Health and personal care items	0.0	 + 1.8 114.0</p>
<p>    Education, entertainment, leisure   + 0.1     + 0.8 109.4</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
